[{:seon.task/name "a-cold-node-decodes-in-one-pass"
  :seon.task/plan "Measured 2026-11-10: the first read of a stored index node costs about 610-750 ticks and 2 KB a datom (69 M of a 94 M-tick scan of 113k ``:form/refs`` datoms was cold decode; the second scan 9.7 M); one konserve read of a small branch head costs 11.7k ticks and 33 KB; the fasl decode of the 17 MB reach graph 37 M ticks. It is the floor under a root's boot (`seon.db/preload!` is 1.2 s of every boot and is decode work), every law that reads the program, the first scan in any test process, and each open. Should cost: at most about 100 ticks and 250 B a datom: its share of one zstd frame, five fields read, one object built (a four-field deftype is 8 ticks and 128 B on the Jolt at upstream's head). Suspected by reading, not measured: a node is decoded into generic vectors and the datoms are built from those afterwards; the leaf's array is grown, not made at its known length; keywords are interned again for each datom. First step: one counted measure of a cold scan split into decompress, fasl read and datom construction, which names the largest; no design before that number. Where: `konserve.jolt.fasl-store`, the node read handlers in `datahike.index.persistent-set`, the sorted set's `restore-node`. Proof when built: a cold scan of n datoms costs a stated number per datom, at sizes to 1,000."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-diff-allocates-only-what-it-answers"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner: Deep fixes. What exists: since Datahike ae20699b (pinned at d32173c3, docs/forks.md#datahike) ``datahike.api/datoms-diff`` of two plain values skips every child stored at an address both hold, compares the rest by Clojure sets and merges the differing leaves once with no lookup in either whole set (docs/storage.md#merges-read-what-changed). Measured with the fix (the Deep fixes session's report, 2026-11-11, on a 250k-datom LMDB store): a 21-datom diff 236k -> 107k ticks warm, 203 values on scattered entities 22.2M -> 2.54M; its cost proof 71.5k, 304k and 1.59M ticks and 289 KB, 1.37 MB and 6.95 MB at 1, 10 and 100 values (seon.merge-cost-test/a-diff-of-two-commits-costs-the-nodes-that-differ). The regression it left: bytes grew 6% and 15% on the scattered cases (reported, not split), from the sets and vectors the new walk builds. Where the bytes go, read in the walk (``reference-code/datahike/src/datahike/index/persistent_set.cljc`` near the diff, and the sorted set's ``.address`` and ``.keys``): each child's address read by a method call, a leaf's keys copied into a fresh vector before the merge, persistent sets built by conj. Correct: read a branch's addresses once (one array a branch); take a leaf's keys without the copy; build the shared-address sets as transients. Proof: the cost proof above with its :per-n bytes lowered to what the fix measures, at or under the pin before's bytes on the scattered cases, seen red first at the lowered bound on d32173c3."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.merge-cost-test/a-diff-of-two-commits-costs-the-nodes-that-differ}}
